  automatedWorkshop:["js/workshop.js:1240-1250 factoryAutomation -> js/buildings.js:1309-1318 Steamworks action()", "PARITY", "**v0.60 PART 5 — RETRIEVED @c52985b, and RR was wrong on ALL THREE of its numbers.** v0.59.1 shipped the SHAPE from a wiki-level description and said so; cloning the source settles it in one grep. `factoryAutomation` carries `effects: {}` and prices science 10,000 + gear 25; the whole mechanism is the Steamworks' action(): `var baseAutomationRate = 0.02; var automationRate = Math.min(baseAutomationRate * (self.on + 1), 0.9); var consumedQuantity = consumedResource.value * automationRate;` triggering on `value >= maxValue * (1 - baseAutomationRate)`. **TRIGGER: 98%, not RR's 0.95. SHARE: min(0.02 x (copies+1), 0.90) of the STOCKPILE — sub-linear and hard-capped — not RR's 0.05 x copies of the CEILING, linear and unbounded. BASE: the current value, not the cap.** RR read ~2x the source at five copies and 100% at twenty against the source's 42%. **The trigger and the share are THE SAME CONSTANT in the source** — an elegant coupling RR had split into two unrelated literals, which is why neither could be made consistent by tuning the other. All three ship: one `AUTOMATION_BASE = 0.02` drives both, the 0.90 cap bites at 44 copies, and the budget is a share of the stockpile. Share table asserted rung for rung: 4 / 6 / 12 / 22 / 42 / 90 percent at 1 / 2 / 5 / 10 / 20 / 44 copies."],
