  hexgateBuilding: ["js/buildings.js:1679 tradepost — `tradeRatio: 0.015` per copy", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** The source funds trade yield from ONE building line; RR funds it from two (Trade Dock and Hexgate) into the same additive category (v0.61 Part 6.1). It also carries a crystal ceiling the tradepost has no analogue for. Two faucets where the source has one is EASIER."],
  marus: ["js/buildings.js temple / ziggurat — the faith production line", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** Devotion is RR's faith analogue and the source funds faith from the Temple line alone. The Maru's Rest is an ADDITIONAL devotion faucet at scale with no counterpart rung, so the same worship curve fills faster. EASIER."],
  piltoverSpire: ["js/buildings.js amphitheatre / chapel — the culture line", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** An extra culture faucet AND an extra culture ceiling on one building, where the source separates the two roles. Its crystal component (v0.53) prices it, but pricing a faucet is not the same as bounding it. EASIER."],
  refinery: ["js/buildings.js calciner — `mineralsPerTickCon` -> `ironPerTickAutoprod: 0.15 * (1 + calcinerRatio)`", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Parts 1 and 3.2 — this is the like-for-like building and it is measured.** The Refinery is a converter exactly as the Calciner is: it consumes per tick and autoproduces per tick, unbounded in count in both games. **Its UPGRADE line is HARDER — three Discoveries summing 0.65 for x1.65 against `calcinerRatio`'s Sigma 2.70 for x3.70, i.e. 45% of the source** — but the delivered product is not, because RR multiplies two further RR-original categories on top (infernal drake x1.495, overseer affinity x2.000, both bounded). **Measured ceiling x4.93 against the source's x3.70: EASIER on the number a player experiences, HARDER on the upgrade line alone.** That distinction is the whole of v0.61 Part 1 and it is why v0.60's x19.77 was wrong."],
  sanctum: ["js/buildings.js templeRatio / `faithRatioReligion`", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** A devotion boost carrier whose contribution passes through `BOOST_LIMIT.devotion = 2.0` and `limitedDR`. **Kittens' faith ratio categories carry no ceiling of this kind** — `<res>RatioReligion` is a plain additive sum. A bounded carrier against an unbounded one is HARDER."],
  shimmerRefinery: ["js/buildings.js calciner (the converter shape)", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** Shimmer has no counterpart resource, so the nearest source-shaped alternative is 'a building that converts one stock into another per tick'. RR runs THREE such lines (Refinery, Shimmer Refinery, Foundry) where the source runs the Calciner and the Smelter. More converter faucets against the same building-count curve is EASIER."],
  vault: ["js/buildings.js warehouse — the second storage tier", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** As `hexcreteBastion`: additional Era-3 ceiling with no counterpart rung and no additional sink. Its crystal component prices the build, not the ceiling."],
  wardOfWatchers: ["no counterpart — nearest shape is a capstone building gated on a terminal tech", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** A Freljord/Void bridge building on a 125,000 capstone. Kittens' terminal buildings sit on rungs two orders of magnitude higher (see the tech rows), so a capstone reachable at RR's 125,000 is EASIER than the source's equivalent by the ladder measurement alone."],
  hexcore: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — alloy (titanium 20 + steel 105) / eludium / thorium", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** No counterpart resource; nearest shape is a crafted intermediate. **RR's Hexcore requires THREE separate chains to converge**, where every Kittens craft draws on one or two inputs. A convergence craft is strictly more constrained than the source's shape: it is gated by whichever chain is furthest behind. HARDER."],
  focusedHex: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — the alloy/eludium refinement shape", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** A refinement step interposed between the crystal converter's output and the buildings that consume it. **Kittens generally spends converter output DIRECTLY** — titanium from the Calciner goes straight into buildings — so an extra mandatory craft between faucet and sink is a step the source does not charge. HARDER."],
  hexSlab: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — the slab/plate shape", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** As `focusedHex`: an extra refinement rung between a converter output and its sink."],
  voidglass: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — eludium (unobtainium 1000)", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** An endgame material behind a terminal tech, requiring its own chain. As `focusedHex`, it interposes a craft where the source often does not."],
  chronoshard: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — the endgame material shape", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** As `voidglass`."],
  runeShard: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — the endgame material shape", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** The World Rune tail; an additional mandatory chain with no counterpart."],
  frostMegalith: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — the endgame material shape", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** The Freljord capstone material; as `voidglass`."],
  petriciteBlock: ["js/workshop.js craft chain — the slab/plate shape", "HARDER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** A stone refinement carrying a crystal cost, which no Kittens stone-line craft does. HARDER on both the extra rung and the extra currency."],
  arcanist: ["js/village.js farmer — the starter-resource job", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1.** Mana is RR's starter faucet and the source's is catnip, worked by farmers. **But RR funds mana from THREE channels where Kittens funds catnip from one**: the Arcanist job, the Mana Well building line, and a manual click channel. Three faucets against one, on the resource the whole opening depends on. EASIER."],
  tinkerer: ["no counterpart — Kittens has NO job producing a converted resource", "EASIER", "**v0.61 Part 3.1, and this one is structural.** Every Kittens converter is a BUILDING; no job in the source produces a converter output. RR adds a job that does, so crystal income scales with population as well as with building count. **A faucet with a second, independent growth term is EASIER by construction** — and it is why v0.60 Part 2's job-loop fix moved crystal income at all."],
